  <h2>Is SimLocal or UPeSIM the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with SimLocal if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want the option of a no-questions refund if the eSIM doesn't work out</li>
        <li>You're headed to the UK and want a real local phone number bundled into the plan, not just data</li>
        <li>You'd rather message support on WhatsApp than dig through a help widget</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with UPeSIM if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want the lower per-GB price on a like-for-like plan</li>
        <li>You're installing the eSIM well ahead of a trip and want it to just sit inactive until you land</li>
        <li>You're fine with a data-only plan and don't need calls, texts, or a refund option</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>SimLocal has physical presence, UPeSIM doesn't.</strong> SimLocal runs a small footprint of staffed airport kiosks, including one at Heathrow, on top of its app and website. UPeSIM is app-and-browser only, like most providers on this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Neither includes calls or texts by default.</strong> UPeSIM is data-only across the board, with roaming calls and SMS routed through your home carrier at whatever rate it charges. SimLocal is also data-only except on most of its UK plans specifically, which bundle a real UK phone number for calls and texts, a detail that doesn't extend to its other destinations.
  </p>
  <p>
    For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>SimLocal vs UPeSIM FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, SimLocal or UPeSIM</h3>
      <p>UPeSIM, per gigabyte, in every destination checked here except Japan, where SimLocal doesn't sell a fixed-GB plan at all. SimLocal's 3GB tiers run roughly 2 to 3 times UPeSIM's 1GB price in the US, Thailand, and UAE.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which one can I get a refund from</h3>
      <p>SimLocal. It advertises a "No Quibble Refunds" policy with no justification required. UPeSIM doesn't publicly offer an equivalent, so treat a UPeSIM purchase as final.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I install either eSIM weeks before my trip</h3>
      <p>Yes for both, since neither starts counting validity until the phone actually connects to the destination network. UPeSIM is explicit that an installed-but-inactive profile expires after 60 days; SimLocal doesn't publish an equivalent limit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does either come with a real phone number</h3>
      <p>Most SimLocal UK plans do, bundling a full UK number for calls and texts. UPeSIM is data-only everywhere, with calls and SMS routed through your home carrier's roaming rates instead.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I talk to a real person in person with either provider</h3>
      <p>Only SimLocal, which runs a small number of staffed airport kiosks, including one at Heathrow. UPeSIM is app-and-browser only.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

